<title>DENMARK: Danish Oct current account surplus 0.2 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish Oct current account surplus 0.2 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account surplus stood at 0.2 billion crowns in October against a revised 2.8 billion crown surplus in September, the national statistics office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods:</p>
<p> (Billions of crowns)	Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p> Current account		  4.5	  7.5	  8.8</p>
<p> Goods				9.7	 20.8	 37.2</p>
<p> Services			   0.8	  4.1	  6.7</p>
<p> Interest, other		 -6.0	-17.8	 -35.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average October current account surplus of 0.5 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
